{title: 544 - Jesus, Son of Blessed Mary}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #544 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 544}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]Jesus, [A]Son [A7]of blessed Mary,
[D/F#]Once [Bm]on [A]earth [A7/G]a [F#m]little [E7/G#]child,
[D/F#]Pattern fair [A/E]of [D]holy [A7]living,
[Bm]Gracious, [F#m]loving, [G]undefiled;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]Though Thy [A]eager [A7]heart was yearning
[D/F#]Heavy [A]laden [F#m]souls [E7/G#]to free,
[D/F#]Yet Thou calledst little [A7]children
[Bm]In [A7/G]their [F#m]happiness [D/F#]to [A/E]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]Grant that [A]we, like [A7]little children,
[D/F#]Free [Bm]from [A]pride [A7/G]and [F#m]guile [E7/G#]my be;
[D/F#]Cheerful, trusting, safe, [A7]protected
[Bm]By [A7/G]the [F#m]blessed [G]Trinity.
{end_of_verse}
